A49 — nudge the session reaper when a guest's window maps or goes away

The reaper (A28) ends the session once no guest image is left, and it learns of
a process exit from SIGCHLD only for the children reparented to it. A game that
stays the child of a live wine process -- the wrapper that started it, explorer
-- exits without a word to the reaper, and only its heartbeat catches that,
seconds later. The compositor sees the exit at once: the game's windows are
unmapped and destroyed when its X connection closes.

So the compositor tells the reaper. Each window records at creation whether its
owner (the X client's pid, from XRes) is a guest image, by the same rule the
reaper applies; a window whose owner is a guest, or is unknown, nudges the
reaper (SIGUSR1) when it maps -- so the first guest is seen the moment its
window shows -- and when it is unmapped or destroyed. The decision is taken at
creation because at destroy time the owner is usually already gone from /proc.
Wine's own windows (the desktop, tabtip) never nudge: their owners fail the
guest rule.

The reaper's pid is the primary child gamescope spawned through the watchdog.
diff --git a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
index adafff0..773e95c 100644
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -5960,6 +5960,14 @@ static void gn_activate_nested_app_window( xwayland_ctx_t *ctx, Window window )
 	if ( hint.res_class ) XFree( hint.res_class );
 }
 
+// A window whose owner is a guest, or whose owner is unknown, is one the
+// session reaper wants to hear about when it maps or goes away.
+static bool
+win_concerns_reaper(const steamcompmgr_win_t *w)
+{
+	return w->pid <= 0 || w->bGuestOwner;
+}
+
 static void
 map_win(xwayland_ctx_t* ctx, Window id, unsigned long sequence)
 {
@@ -5969,6 +5977,8 @@ map_win(xwayland_ctx_t* ctx, Window id, unsigned long sequence)
 		return;
 
 	w->xwayland().a.map_state = IsViewable;
+	if (win_concerns_reaper(w))
+		gamescope::Process::KickSessionReaper();
 
 	/* This needs to be here or else we lose transparency messages */
 	XSelectInput(ctx->dpy, id, PropertyChangeMask | SubstructureNotifyMask |
@@ -6090,6 +6100,8 @@ unmap_win(xwayland_ctx_t *ctx, Window id, bool fade)
 	if (!w)
 		return;
 	w->xwayland().a.map_state = IsUnmapped;
+	if (win_concerns_reaper(w))
+		gamescope::Process::KickSessionReaper();
 
 	MakeFocusDirty();
 
@@ -6211,6 +6223,7 @@ add_win(xwayland_ctx_t *ctx, Window id, Window prev, unsigned long sequence)
 	{
 		new_win->pid = -1;
 	}
+	new_win->bGuestOwner = gamescope::Process::IsGuestProcess( new_win->pid );
 
 	new_win->isOverlay = false;
 	new_win->isExternalOverlay = false;
@@ -6459,7 +6472,11 @@ finish_destroy_win(xwayland_ctx_t *ctx, Window id, bool gone)
 		if (w->xwayland().id == id)
 		{
 			if (gone)
+			{
 				finish_unmap_win (ctx, w);
+				if (win_concerns_reaper(w))
+					gamescope::Process::KickSessionReaper();
+			}
 			
 			{
 				std::unique_lock lock( ctx->list_mutex );
@@ -9620,6 +9637,7 @@ void LaunchNestedChildren( char **ppPrimaryChildArgv )
 	if ( ppPrimaryChildArgv && *ppPrimaryChildArgv )
 	{
 		pid_t nPrimaryChildPid = gamescope::Process::SpawnProcessInWatchdog( ppPrimaryChildArgv, false );
+		gamescope::Process::SetSessionReaper( nPrimaryChildPid );
 
 		std::thread waitThread([ nPrimaryChildPid ]()
 		{
